From 64bd6a4591332b6a546245e20ba168084713c6cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luannt <luannt.devops@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:07:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(config,backend,cmd): one workspace and one data dir per
 repository

A repository could end up with two crush.db depending on which directory
was opened first (sub before root), a symlink into a subdirectory put the
data dir outside the repo, and repo and repo/sub became two workspaces on
one database, so one session could run two turns at once. Every mode now
resolves one project root (physical git toplevel, one shared function):
the workspace, its data dir and the process working directory are the
root, also when opened from a subdirectory (user decision 20/10). Older
.crush directories are kept and reported (registry `locations` is kept
for reading; warning from root, subdirectory and Home) instead of merged.
`loop` keeps running --verify where it was started, names that directory
in the prompt and fingerprints the whole repo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
